  "summary": "Manual-transmission shifter boots and the backdrive (ignition-lock interlock) cable. The upper shift boot [2] goes on with screws [1] at the console shifter opening (remove the shift knob first); the lower boot [4] screws [3] onto plate [5], which is riveted [6] to the floor tunnel. Backdrive cable [12] runs from a bracket [11] bolted (two bolts [9]) on the transmission to the lever on the steering column; at each end the cable housing is clipped with retainer [10] and the inner wire end is held in its lever with washer [7] and cotter pin [8].",
